Chapter Two: Jesus Heals a Paralytic
And after some days, Jesus returned to Capernaum, and the people heard that he was at home.
A lot of people gathered, so much that there was no space left in front of the door. He began teaching them the words of God.
They brought him a paralyzed man carried by four men.
And when they couldn't get close to him because of the crowd, they tore open the roof above the place where he was sitting, made an opening, and lowered the bed where the paralyzed man was sleeping.
And when Jesus saw their faith, he said to the paralyzed man, "Son, your sins are forgiven!"
And the wise men said something about the knowledge of the law, and they thought to themselves:
